This project was designed with reference to, and borrows ideas from, the
following open-source projects. No source files were copied verbatim; the
approaches below were re-implemented for automotive repair use.

1. claude-code-youtube-extract
   https://github.com/muckybuzzwoo/claude-code-youtube-extract
   Copyright (c) Mucky / buzzwoo — Apache License 2.0
   Ideas used: packaging as a Claude Code plugin + skill backed by a Python
   script; yt-dlp metadata/caption retrieval; ffmpeg scene-score frame
   detection (`select='gt(scene,T)'`) with a minimum gap; perceptual
   de-duplication of near-identical frames via tiny grayscale thumbnails.

2. youtube-practice-guide
   https://github.com/LongJingSU/youtube-practice-guide
   Copyright (c) LongJingSU — MIT License
   Ideas used: contact sheets of timestamped frames for the model to review;
   the "guide supplements the video, it doesn't replace it" principle with a
   timestamp on every step; self-contained HTML output with embedded images
   alongside archival Markdown.

Third-party runtime dependencies (installed separately, not bundled):
  yt-dlp (Unlicense), imageio-ffmpeg (BSD-2-Clause; downloads an LGPL/GPL
  FFmpeg build), Pillow (MIT-CMU), pydantic (MIT), faster-whisper (MIT,
  optional), onnxruntime (MIT, optional).
